{
  "name": "v96_search",
  "_why": [
    "The general search tune for v9.6, from batch H's values: every search",
    "parameter the v9.5 batches added or left untouched since v9.1. Left out:",
    "time management, tuned on its own at 10+0.1; the whole-ply LMR adjustments",
    "and IIR's reduction, set by measurement in batch E and too coarse for SPSA;",
    "the TT settings, which only matter under table pressure at long controls;",
    "and the fifty-move and material scaling, rarely active or switched off.",
    "",
    "c_end is about a twentieth of each parameter's sensible range, so moving",
    "one by c_end costs a few Elo (METHODOLOGY 10). 0.5 is the tuner's floor for",
    "small integers. The engine is the batch H SPRT binary with its net compiled",
    "in, so SGR_EVALFILE must be unset and the binary left alone while this runs."
  ],
  "engine": "sgurr_cpp/sprt_batch_h.exe",
  "book": "testing/8moves_v3.pgn",
  "book_format": "pgn",
  "tc": "8+0.08",
